# Database Rules

## Tables

`Users`, `Customers`, `Bookings`, `Sales`, `Reports`, `EmailLogs`

## Conventions

- Use `INT AUTO_INCREMENT` primary keys
- `created_at`, `updated_at` timestamps on all tables
- Foreign keys with `ON DELETE` behavior documented
- Index columns used in analytics queries (event_date, status, package_id)

## Key Relationships

- `Bookings` → `Customers` (customer info)
- `Sales` → `Bookings` (completed booking revenue)
- `EmailLogs` → `Bookings` or `Customers` (notification audit trail)
- `Reports` — stores generated report metadata and file paths

## Booking Status Flow

`pending` → `approved` / `rejected` → `completed` (triggers retention record + future anniversary email)

## Security

- Parameterized queries only — no string concatenation for SQL
- Passwords hashed with bcrypt in `Users` table
